        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): reject zero-value cron.sessionRetention to prevent silent data loss",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nConfiguring `cron.sessionRetention: \"0h\"` (or `\"0d\"`, `\"0ms\"`) is silently accepted by Zod config validation. `parseDurationMs(\"0h\")` returns `0` without throwing, so the `superRefine` passes the value. `resolveRetentionMs` returns `0ms` with no guard, and `sweepCronRunSessions` computes `cutoff = now - 0 = now`, matching all cron run sessions for immediate deletion.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Schema gate (prevention)**: Added `ms <= 0` guard in `superRefine` to reject zero-duration strings at config validation time.\n\n**Doctor migration (upgrade safety)**: Added a registered legacy rule + migration so existing installations with zero-duration values accepted by `v2026.6.11` auto-recover via `openclaw doctor --fix`. The migration removes only zero-duration strings (`\"0h\"`, `\"0d\"`, `\"0ms\"`) so the documented 24h default applies; positive durations and `false` (documented disable) are preserved.\n\n### Files changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/config/zod-schema.ts` | +11/-3: reject zero-duration in superRefine |\n| `src/config/schema.test.ts` | +12: schema regression cases |\n| `src/commands/doctor/shared/legacy-config-migrations.runtime.cron.ts` | +45: rule + migration spec |\n| `src/commands/doctor/shared/legacy-config-migrations.runtime.cron.test.ts` | +118: 14 focused tests |\n| `src/commands/doctor/shared/legacy-config-migrations.runtime.ts` | +2: register cron migration |\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n### Migration + Schema + Integration tests (all passing)\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor/shared/legacy-config-migrations.runtime.cron.test.ts\nTests  14 passed (14)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/schema.test.ts\nTests  59 passed (59)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor-legacy-config.migrations.test.ts\nTests  63 passed (63)\n```\n\n### Doctor detection → repair → validation (end-to-end)\n\n```\n$ echo '{\"agents\":{\"list\":[{\"id\":\"main\"}]},\"cron\":{\"sessionRetention\":\"0h\"}}' > /tmp/zero-retention.json5\n\n$ OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=/tmp/zero-retention.json5 pnpm --silent openclaw doctor --fix --yes\n```\n\nDoctor detects the issue via the registered legacy rule:\n\n```\nLegacy config keys detected:\n\n- cron: cron.sessionRetention is a zero duration — this causes\n  immediate deletion of all cron run sessions. Run \"openclaw doctor\n  --fix\" to remove it so the documented 24h default applies.\n```\n\nDoctor applies the migration:\n\n```\nDoctor changes:\n\nRemoved cron.sessionRetention \"0h\" (zero duration); documented 24h\ndefault applies.\n```\n\nConfig file after fix — `sessionRetention` removed, documented 24h default applies:\n\n```\n$ cat /tmp/zero-retention.json5 | jq .cron\n{\"maxConcurrentRuns\": 8}\n```\n\nConfig validation passes after migration:\n\n```\n$ OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=/tmp/zero-retention.json5 pnpm --silent openclaw config validate --json\n{\"valid\":true,\"path\":\"/tmp/zero-retention.json5\",\"warnings\":[]}\n```\n\n### Before fix: zero values rejected (schema gate working)\n\n```\n$ echo '{\"agents\":{\"list\":[{\"id\":\"main\"}]},\"cron\":{\"sessionRetention\":\"0h\"}}' > /tmp/cfg-zero.json5\n$ OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=/tmp/cfg-zero.json5 pnpm --silent openclaw config validate --json\n{\n  \"valid\": false,\n  \"issues\": [{\n    \"path\": \"cron.sessionRetention\",\n    \"message\": \"duration must be positive (use ms, s, m, h, d), e.g. 24h\"\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n### Diff whitespace checks\n\n`git diff --check` passed.\n\n- **Not tested / proof gaps**: None.",
